  "notes": "Official 2025-2026 Curriculum Roadmap for the Marine Transportation major (Students Entering in 2025, dated 04/22/25). The roadmap prints 'THIRD MATE'S/OICNW LICENSE REQUIRED FOR GRADUATION'. Students are assigned to Divisions 1&2 or 3&4; the roadmap marks the alternating courses and this seed follows the Divisions 1&2 placement (first-listed on the roadmap): FF 100 in Fall 2025 (Divisions 3&4 take it in Spring 2026); in Fall 2027 Divisions 1&2 take the Arts Elective and DL 301 while Divisions 3&4 take the GWAR; in Spring 2028 Divisions 1&2 take the GWAR and Divisions 3&4 take the Arts Elective and DL 301; in Fall 2028 Divisions 1&2 take DL 405, DL 405L and DL 410 while Divisions 3&4 take DL 305 and NAU 415; in Spring 2029 the swap reverses. Both division tracks total 148 units. PE 102 Beginning/Intermediate Swimming is printed as (0.5) and excluded from the printed 18.0 Fall 2025 total. Bracketed lines (e.g. '[Critical Thinking Elective] (Area 1B)', '[American Institutions II Elective] (Area 4-Lower Div)') are GE-area annotations on the course above, not separate courses. PHY 100 Physics I (1.0) and PHY 100L Physics I Lab (3.0) units are printed verbatim as on the roadmap. 0.0-unit courses (DL 105X, FF 100, FF 300, PE 101) are genuine 0-credit requirements. No course-level prerequisites are printed on the roadmap.",
